# Mercury 3 — findings by MiniMax M3.1 Flash

- Source: Inception (mercury-3)
- Date: 2026-11-12 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury 3
- **Short description:** Inception Labs' flagship diffusion LLM (dLLM): a masked-diffusion decoder that refines many tokens in parallel instead of emitting them one by one, delivering reasoning-grade answers at roughly 1,000 tokens per second with a 1M-token context window. Not an alias — this is the distinct October 2026 generation, 40x larger in total parameters than Mercury 1 (vendor claim) and the successor to Mercury 2 and Mercury 2.5.
- **Provider / access:** Inception API, OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions at `https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1/chat/completions` with model id `mercury-3`; also served via OpenRouter (`inception/mercury-3`), Baseten and Vercel. Streaming is supported; a diffusion "denoising" visualization mode is documented. No OpenCode Zen route exists — the OpenCode Console model catalog lists no Mercury model.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-10-19 (Inception launch post; Vals AI model record also gives 2026-10-19; OpenRouter lists 2026-10-16). Knowledge cutoff not disclosed by the vendor.
- **IDs:** `inception/mercury-3` (OpenRouter / Benchize canonical slug `inception/mercury-3-20261019`), `mercury-3` (Inception API). No free Zen ID exists.
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 tokens total, up to 131,072 max output tokens — verified on the Inception models-and-pricing doc, the OpenRouter model page, and the Vals AI model record (1M context, 131k max output).
- **Modalities:** text in / text out only. Reasoning: yes, with `reasoning_effort` values `instant`, `low`, `medium` and `high` (default `low`); temperature adjustable 0.5–1.0. Tool calling: yes, OpenAI-compatible, including parallel tool calls. Structured outputs: yes (JSON schema via `response_format`). No image, audio, video or PDF input — Vals AI records image input as unsupported and the Inception model table lists supported format `Text`.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-12):** launch price $0.10 per 1M input tokens and $0.35 per 1M output tokens (50% off), cached input $0.01; regular list price $0.20 in / $0.70 out, cached $0.02. Paid model, but every new Inception API key ships with 100 million free tokens (free tier rate limits: 1,000 requests, 1M input tokens and 100k output tokens per minute); enterprise deployments can configure data retention.
- **Architecture:** proprietary diffusion LLM — masked-diffusion parallel decoding, not autoregressive; parameter count not disclosed (vendor states only that it is more than 40x Mercury 1 in total parameters).

